+# Unverified Wave 3 checkpoint
+
+Base e54523517d0f03e58352e647c403a5af3e525a57.
+Branch research/continuous-20261110-crt-rows.
+Started implementation at2026-11-10 17:03 UTC under a70+20minute bound.
+
+The current code replaces only the compiled selection/header/target fragment
+of #5496. It retains actual numerical Entry/Bank, the unchanged ROM program
+and execute, and exact copy/skip/countdown primitives. It borrows a unary
+encoded ell. No ell=max-width inference or complete source installer is used.
+The pinned node frontend is retained from public CubeJerry commit
+cc35ecedce6f208d5056fab6d17c58555affc73c. Its public advancing lease is not
+reused: the new row iterator closes the actual numerical Bank Lease, clears
+the pending marker while retaining STEP, and advances the node once after
+the final global row. This interface still needs independent review.
+
+Executed smoke coverage: five real rows on d2, widths3/2, ell3, including
+two literal idles and three actual ROM invocations (8,330,780 instructions).
+A second actual prefix executes seven rows on d4, widths3/3/2/2: all first
+node rows followed by two rows at nonzero start2. Host geometry functions
+are poisoned and physical constructors sealed after initial acquisition.
+Its actual ROM count is218,784,440. These smoke runs are not yet the frozen
+oracle verification receipt and do not establish the universal theorem.
+
+Current inventory is137 owned roles:78 inherited numerical/node/guard roles,
+52 ROM/header,3 query,4 row selectors. The source and encoded ell are two
+additional borrowed roles. All histories must be checked in the next stage.
+
+Remaining: independent arithmetic selector oracle, exact source/ell snapshots,
+historical-capacity and lifecycle checks, meaningful controls, source pins,
+full source-operation proof/invoice, registered metadata/tests, cross-review
+and publication checks. Source production, encoded-ell production, coordinate
+installation, full payload permutation and binary lowering remain open.
+
+Next command will be the package verifier once written. This checkpoint is
+explicitly unverified and is not a publication candidate.
